---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConsultForm from '../components/ConsultForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Board AI Algorithmic Accountability Advisory | Lozen Advisory" description="Board-facing advisory on AI incidents, accountability gaps, Caremark oversight, D&O exposure, reputation risk, and what the operating record can prove.">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="grid-bg"></div>
  <div class="wrap inner">
    <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="/#services">Services</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Algorithmic Accountability Risk</div>
    <span class="pill">Crisis, Reputation & Accountability</span>
    <div class="ic-lg"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:52px;height:52px;color:var(--accent-2)"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div>
    <h1>Algorithmic Accountability Risk</h1>
    <p class="sub">Caremark oversight, D&O exposure, and insurance underwriting now ask the same question: who was accountable, and can the organization prove it?</p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a href="#consult" class="btn btn-accent">Discuss This Engagement →</a>
      <a href="#how" class="btn btn-ghost">How it works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
      <h2 class="h2">When the incident happens, the accountability record has to hold.</h2>
      <p>AI incidents become board, financial, legal, and reputation events when authority and evidence are unclear.</p>
      <p>Lozen Advisory helps leadership determine what happened, who owned the decision, what the record proves, and where the governance failure sits.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="checklist" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Board and committee accountability analysis</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Caremark oversight exposure</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>D&O and insurance implications</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Human-attribution assessment</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Incident and decision-chain reconstruction</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Board-ready advisory findings</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What's included</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Everything in this service</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div><h3>Accountability map</h3><p>Identify the human, institutional, and system actors connected to the decision.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"/><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"/><line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"/></svg></div><h3>Evidence review</h3><p>Assess what the operating record establishes and what remains unsupported.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg></div><h3>Authority analysis</h3><p>Determine who had the power to approve, constrain, escalate, or refuse.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg></div><h3>Board exposure</h3><p>Translate the incident into oversight, committee, and governance questions.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></div><h3>Financial risk</h3><p>Surface D&O, insurance, disclosure, and liability implications.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg></div><h3>Advisory findings</h3><p>Provide a concise board-facing analysis of the accountability failure.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="h2">A clear advisory process</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Scope</h3><p>Define the incident, decision, or emerging accountability concern.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Examine</h3><p>Review the authority structure, evidence, escalation path, and operating record.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Translate</h3><p>Connect the findings to board, CFO, legal, risk, and insurance exposure.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">4</div><h3>Brief</h3><p>Deliver the findings and the questions leadership must resolve next.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Is this an incident-response service?</h4><p>No. It is a governance and accountability advisory engagement focused on what the incident reveals about authority, evidence, and oversight.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Can this be used before an incident?</h4><p>Yes. The same analysis can test whether current accountability structures would hold up before failure forces the question.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Who should be involved?</h4><p>Boards, CFOs, General Counsel, risk leaders, corporate secretaries, and executives accountable for AI use or its consequences.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<ConsultForm serviceHighlight="algorithmic accountability risk" selectedService="Algorithmic Accountability Risk" />
</BaseLayout>
